<title>USA: South Korean Ex-Im Bank files shelf $2.0 bln debt.</title>
<headline>South Korean Ex-Im Bank files shelf $2.0 bln debt.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The South Korean Export-Import Bank filed a shelf registration Thursday with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission for up to $2.0 billion in debt securities and warrants to purchase debt securities.</p>
<p>When combined with previous registrations, the South Korean institution will have up to $2.24 billion in debt securities available for sale, according to the filing.</p>
<p>The government agency said it will use net proceeds for its general funding purposes, including the repayment of foreign currency obligations and the making of foreign currency loans.</p>
</text>
